  "label": "the overallintent",
  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The meme uses a three-panel format featuring a man in a suit holding a briefcase, mimicking the iconic 'I'm from the group' scene from the movie 'The Matrix' (where the character Neo is often portrayed as a 'group' member). The first panel says 'don't shoot, i'm from the group,' the second panel shows armed tactical personnel with the text 'why dont you post and comment?', and the third panel returns to the man in the suit with 'i'm shy, but i like stuff.' The overall intent is to humorously and ironically portray online users who are hesitant to engage in social media discussions or comment sections, despite having an interest in the subject matter. The meme is not targeting any specific group based on protected characteristics, nor does it contain abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynous, or propaganda elements. The humor stems from the contrast between the man's passive, almost apologetic demeanor and the aggressive context of the armed personnel, which is used to satirize the reluctance of some people to participate in online discourse. The intent is to create a relatable and light-hearted commentary on social media behavior, not to cause harm or promote negativity.",
